{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/764197-hegemony-pure-2e","id":764197,"title":"Hegemony (Pure 2e)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-12T10:48:42-08:00","id":764197,"title":"Hegemony (Pure 2e)","content":"The following is my idea of how to use the Pure in a chronicle. The idea is to create a set of antagonists who can cooperate with Forsaken much of time while still having a consistently sinister agenda. The goal of the Pure is to dominate Ghost Wolves and Forsaken by reminding them of their inferiority, treating them as second or third class, and to consistently undermine them.<br /> <br /> They can't just kill The Forsaken, they have to show that they were wrong for opposing the Pure in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hegemony<br /> <br /> The Pure have two distinct advantages over the Forsaken which allows them to exploit them rather than treat them simply as a vicious enemy. The Pure outnumber the Forsaken and have expressed only vague statements about their sacred prey.<br /> <br /> The fact that they are numerous, have large packs, and have more allies in the Shadow allows for them to comfortably interact with the Pure from a position of power. This allows them to treat the Forsaken as a minority that at times can be exploited. The Forsaken are seen as lesser, backwards, moon-crazed, and collectively guilty, however they are still Uratha. If there is a Beshilu epidemic in the region or an Idigam, a pack of nine or ten Predator Kings may conscript four or five Hunters in the Darkness in order to fight for them. In these hunts the conscripted Forsaken are treated at best as enlisted troops and at worse hounds only good for their noses with no say.<br /> <br /> This has multiple benefits. The first is that conscripted Uratha can die while their pack members live. The second is that the Forsaken tend to specialize more closely in hunting certain types of prey and have gifts and rites which aid them in this. The third is that in hunting with the Pure, any Forsaken conscripts may be seduced by their prowess and may consider joining the pure.<br /> <br /> While the Forsaken hunt particular types of supernatural threats as their sacred prey, the Pure seem to hunt those who transgress against their value system. This allows them to include the Forsaken as their sacred prey. It also allows them to be flexible in who they hunt, meaning that they can avoid hunting the Forsaken and can even justify intervening in the Forsaken affairs in a non-hostile manner.<br /> <br /> For the Ivory Claws, &quot;Those do not honor their lineage are the sacred prey of the tribe <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">\u2014 which, by most Ivory </span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Claw definitions, includes all of the Forsaken.</span></span></span></span>&quot; (Werewolf: The Forsaken 2nd Edition, 197). This can be twisted around in many ways. Ivory Claws may keep their genocidal intentions hidden and begin to claim that their true goal is the protection of wolf bloods and to prevent spirits from infecting Wolf Bloods and human servants with genetic disease.<br /> <br /> The Fire-Touched on the other hand claim to hunt those who dishonor and disrespect the Shadow. This does in their mind include the Forsaken. However it might also include Mages, Beasts, or Sorcerous Vampires who attempt to steal the secrets of the Shadows. With this in mind they may use this as an excuse to interfere in the affairs of the Forsaken offering unwanted assistance and advice.<br /> <br /> The Predator Kings offer a romantic view of the world and portray themselves as protectors of the Hunt and wish the return of Pangaea. They portray themselves quite openly as defenders of the natural order. Their Wolf Bloods try to protect, expand, purchase, and influence wild life reserves and national parks so that the Predator Kings can keep the wild places alive. This romanticism is extremely attractive to many Forsaken.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","user":"AForgeForThoughts","date":".  Title Flair 11-12-2015, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T13:05:58-08:00","id":765736,"title":"","content":"For mine non-one sided take on Pure I go with other assumptions. Yours idea sounds more as &quot;Pure enlist stupid Forsaken as shock troopers&quot;. Mine is &quot;convert Forsaken by our actions&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/764197-hegemony-pure-2e#post764197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The following is my idea of how to use the Pure in a chronicle. The idea is to create a set of antagonists who can cooperate with Forsaken much of time while still having a consistently sinister agenda. The goal of the Pure is to dominate Ghost Wolves and Forsaken by reminding them of their inferiority, treating them as second or third class, and to consistently undermine them.<br /> <br /> They can't just kill The Forsaken, they have to show that they were wrong for opposing the Pure in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the problem - you cannot convince anyone when treating them with disrespect. Would you agree with me, on core level, when I would insult you? I bet you would not.<br /> <br /> No, for Pure to covert Forsaken you must show other way. You must point your common elements. You must... show them the Wolf. Pure wanting to convert other Uratha must prove that Wolf's intention was <b>not </b>for his children to follow Moon. Pure need to be &quot;purest of wolves&quot; that upholds virtues of Wolf higher than Forsaken - and doing it damn good!<br /> <br /> Evil for evil sake werewolves are Bale Hounds. If Pure want to succeed in their conversions, they need to seem paragons for other Uratha to strive for, not mindless fanatics that only cut their own Spirit Brands. Converting Pure must be silver tongues, but also be perfectionists in the way they fulfill their Oaths of the Wolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/764197-hegemony-pure-2e#post764197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure have two distinct advantages over the Forsaken which allows them to exploit them rather than treat them simply as a vicious enemy. The Pure outnumber the Forsaken and have expressed only vague statements about their sacred prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>As history shows ( see <b>Dark Eras</b> and history section of <b>Pure</b> books ) the rise and fall of Pure numbers goes in cycles. Last Bretheren War of 90's was result from overpopulation of Forsaken, and that packs did not had space. Literally, Tribes of Moon were too high in numbers for their own good. The in-fights started and brother killed brother. From there, Pure just used situation.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly last large Pure rise were in the <i><b>Bowery Dogs </b></i>in <b>Dark Eras</b>, the 1970s. From there there was decline, spring of Forsaken - until they started to hunt one another and starting of Brethren War. This cycle repeats all and all over again - so &quot;Pure have large numbers&quot; is not really convincing argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/764197-hegemony-pure-2e#post764197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that they are numerous, have large packs, and have more allies in the Shadow allows for them to comfortably interact with the Pure from a position of power. This allows them to treat the Forsaken as a minority that at times can be exploited. The Forsaken are seen as lesser, backwards, moon-crazed, and collectively guilty, however they are still Uratha. If there is a Beshilu epidemic in the region or an Idigam, a pack of nine or ten Predator Kings may conscript four or five Hunters in the Darkness in order to fight for them. In these hunts the conscripted Forsaken are treated at best as enlisted troops and at worse hounds only good for their noses with no say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good spirits standing <b>is</b> convincing argument - only remember that showing Forsaken as &quot;crazy&quot; do not work for the conversions. BUT pointing that Luna is Mad Goddess from the <b><i>out of our planet</i></b><i>(!)</i> - sure can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-14-2015, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T13:07:22-08:00","id":765739,"title":"","content":"I am liking this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Now, all we need are Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T14:37:10-08:00","id":765805,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the feedback. I will attempt to defend my ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/764197-hegemony-pure-2e?p=765736#post765736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yours idea sounds more as &quot;Pure enlist stupid Forsaken as shock troopers&quot;. Mine is &quot;convert Forsaken by our actions&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forced conscription or military service in exchange for a second class status has been used by many empires in history. Both the Romans and the Ottomans did this in very different ways. I do not think that the Forsaken would be stupid to go along with conscription or forced hunts if they were threatened in the correct way. This could be anything from &quot;Join or die&quot; to &quot;If do this hunt with us it will gain a year long peace treaty&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janissaries\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Lambert_Wyts_-_Agha_of_the_Janissaries_and_a_B%C3%B6l%C3%BCk_of_the_Janissaries.jpg/960px-Lambert_Wyts_-_Agha_of_the_Janissaries_and_a_B%C3%B6l%C3%BCk_of_the_Janissaries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janissaries\" target=\"_blank\"> Janissary - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janissaries\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janissaries </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auxilia\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Engineering_corps_traian_s_column_river_crossing.jpg/1280px-Engineering_corps_traian_s_column_river_crossing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auxilia\" target=\"_blank\"> Auxilia - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auxilia\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auxilia </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/764197-hegemony-pure-2e?p=765736#post765736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the problem - you cannot convince anyone when treating them with disrespect. Would you agree with me, on core level, when I would insult you? I bet you would not.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI do not think that this is true at all. People use bullying all the time to get people to change their opinions. In particular though I was attempting to incorporate the horror's of cultural genocide into the pure. As group of people with hegemony this is the next step.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultural_genocide\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/11/Warsaw_1944_by_Ba%C5%82uk_-_26320.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultural_genocide\" target=\"_blank\"> Cultural genocide - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultural_genocide\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultural_genocide </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This can and does easily backfire of course, but the pure don't need to be completely rational.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/764197-hegemony-pure-2e?p=765736#post765736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As history shows ( see <b>Dark Eras</b> and history section of <b>Pure</b> books ) the rise and fall of Pure numbers goes in cycles. Last Bretheren War of 90's was result from overpopulation of Forsaken, and that packs did not had space. Literally, Tribes of Moon were too high in numbers for their own good. The in-fights started and brother killed brother. From there, Pure just used situation.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly last large Pure rise were in the <i><b>Bowery Dogs </b></i>in <b>Dark Eras</b>, the 1970s. From there there was decline, spring of Forsaken - until they started to hunt one another and starting of Brethren War. This cycle repeats all and all over again - so &quot;Pure have large numbers&quot; is not really convincing argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is interesting. I am mostly basing this off of the second edition book, which is where I got the impression that the Pure were meant to be used as an enemy that has greater numbers. Obviously if they had smaller numbers their role and tactics would change, which is fine. Greater numbers are not the intrinsic property of a group of werewolves. This is true, and I imagine that if and when the Pure's numbers shrink they may completely change tactics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/764197-hegemony-pure-2e?p=765736#post765736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, for Pure to covert Forsaken you must show other way. You must point your common elements. You must... show them the Wolf. Pure wanting to convert other Uratha must prove that Wolf's intention was <b>not </b>for his children to follow Moon. Pure need to be &quot;purest of wolves&quot; that upholds virtues of Wolf higher than Forsaken - and doing it damn good!<br /> <br /> Evil for evil sake werewolves are Bale Hounds. If Pure want to succeed in their conversions, they need to seem paragons for other Uratha to strive for, not mindless fanatics that only cut their own Spirit Brands. Converting Pure must be silver tongues, but also be perfectionists in the way they fulfill their Oaths of the Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I suggested mindless fanatics or anything like Bale Hounds. The exact thing I want to do is avoid &quot;Monster's monsters&quot;. As I indicated in my original post, I think that each Pure tribe has something to offer when it comes to leading by example. I think however if they do this they will be more like rivals that horror antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T14:45:44-08:00","id":765812,"title":"","content":"Interesting that you bring up the Romans, as the proposed idea for the Forsaken in Rome Dark Era involves a look at the Uratha as part of one of the Empire's 'slave' nations. Though I hope we can step away from the werewolves-as-barbarians trope.<br /> <br /> I like your ideas, though I don't think they're for everyone, some do seem to want a more clear threat and prefer to have the Pure as just evil antagonists akin to orcs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T15:45:51-08:00","id":765843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/764197-hegemony-pure-2e?p=765805#post765805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forced conscription or military service in exchange for a second class status has been used by many empires in history. Both the Romans and the Ottomans did this in very different ways. I do not think that the Forsaken would be stupid to go along with conscription or forced hunts if they were threatened in the correct way. This could be anything from &quot;Join or die&quot; to &quot;If do this hunt with us it will gain a year long peace treaty&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janissaries\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Lambert_Wyts_-_Agha_of_the_Janissaries_and_a_B%C3%B6l%C3%BCk_of_the_Janissaries.jpg/960px-Lambert_Wyts_-_Agha_of_the_Janissaries_and_a_B%C3%B6l%C3%BCk_of_the_Janissaries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janissaries\" target=\"_blank\"> Janissary - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janissaries\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janissaries </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auxilia\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Engineering_corps_traian_s_column_river_crossing.jpg/1280px-Engineering_corps_traian_s_column_river_crossing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auxilia\" target=\"_blank\"> Auxilia - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auxilia\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auxilia </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I do not think that this is true at all. People use bullying all the time to get people to change their opinions. In particular though I was attempting to incorporate the horror's of cultural genocide into the pure. As group of people with hegemony this is the next step.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultural_genocide\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/11/Warsaw_1944_by_Ba%C5%82uk_-_26320.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultural_genocide\" target=\"_blank\"> Cultural genocide - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultural_genocide\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultural_genocide </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This can and does easily backfire of course, but the pure don't need to be completely rational.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably also include leveraging hostages in that department. As - even with Wolf-Blooded being elevated in their roles as of 2e - the Pure can still take advantage of the Forsaken's human kin to force their cooperation. On a related note, it's equally plausible for the Wolf-Blooded of a Forsaken Pack to take the Pure up on their offer if they justify it as a way of protecting their werewolf cousins.<br /> <br /> And on the topic of cultural genocide, taking the Forsaken out via their Wolf-Blooded also rings strongly with the concept. The Fire-Touched and Ivory Claws would be the most likely to favor this tactic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/764197-hegemony-pure-2e?p=765812#post765812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting that you bring up the Romans, as the proposed idea for the Forsaken in Rome Dark Era involves a look at the Uratha as part of one of the Empire's 'slave' nations. Though I hope we can step away from the werewolves-as-barbarians trope.<br /> <br /> I like your ideas, though I don't think they're for everyone, some do seem to want a more clear threat and prefer to have the Pure as just evil antagonists akin to orcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason, I had this strong Underworld vibe when you mentioned that Dark Eras tidbit. I even got an image in my head of the Camarilla making use of Uratha serfs in a manner similar to how Underworld's vampires used the Lycans as slaves in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T23:15:11-08:00","id":766083,"title":"","content":"Oh man, I can't wait for you guys to see what I and a few others have cooked up in the Forsaken by Rome Dark Era! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can tell you - surely without risking the NDA-ninjas! - that I was *all over* Wikipedia's sources about the Auxilia. And I'm pretty sure that we've avoided the &quot;werewolves = barbarians&quot; trope, too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}